1	# Contract: `ChatRepository`/`ChatRepositoryImpl`/`ChatLocalCache` bookmark extension
2	
3	Extends the interface `specs/007-chat-memory-rag/contracts/chat-repository.md` already defines (every
4	existing member unchanged) with the one new read/write pair FR-008 needs — a device-local, best-effort record
5	of which chat messages have already produced an entry (research.md R1).
6	
7	```dart
8	abstract class ChatRepository {
9	  // createSession / listSessions / cachedSessions / listMessages / cachedMessages /
10	  // setLastActiveSessionId / lastActiveSessionId / sendMessage / retryMessage — unchanged
11	
12	  String? savedEntryIdFor(String chatMessageId);
13	
14	  Future<void> recordMessageSaved({required String chatMessageId, required String entryId});
15	}
16	```
17	
18	## `ChatLocalCache` additions (data layer)
19	
20	```dart
21	static const _savedMessageEntryIdsKey = 'chatSavedMessageEntryIds';   // 4th independent key
22	
23	Future<Map<String, String>> readSavedMessageEntryIds() async {
24	  final raw = await _storage.read(key: _savedMessageEntryIdsKey);
25	  if (raw == null) return const {};
26	  try {
27	    final decoded = jsonDecode(raw) as Map<String, dynamic>;
28	    return decoded.map((k, v) => MapEntry(k, v as String));
29	  } on FormatException {
30	    return const {};
31	  } on TypeError {
32	    return const {};
33	  }
34	}
35	
36	Future<void> writeSavedMessageEntryIds(Map<String, String> ids) {
37	  return _storage.write(key: _savedMessageEntryIdsKey, value: jsonEncode(ids));
38	}
39	```
40	
41	Same malformed-data-returns-empty fallback shape every other `ChatLocalCache`/`EntriesLocalCache` read method
42	already uses — a corrupted or unreadable record degrades to "nothing known saved yet," never a crash; the
43	backend's own idempotency (not this cache) is what still prevents a duplicate entry if that happens (research.md
44	R1).
45	
46	## `ChatRepositoryImpl` additions (data layer)
47	
48	```dart
49	Map<String, String> _savedMessageEntryIds = {};
50	
51	Future<void> _ensureLocalCacheLoaded() {
52	  return _localCacheLoad ??= () async {
53	    _cachedSessions = await _localCache.readSessions();
54	    _cachedMessages.addAll(await _localCache.readAllMessages());
55	    _savedMessageEntryIds = await _localCache.readSavedMessageEntryIds();   // NEW line in the existing future
56	  }();
57	}
58	
59	@override
60	String? savedEntryIdFor(String chatMessageId) => _savedMessageEntryIds[chatMessageId];
61	
62	@override
63	Future<void> recordMessageSaved({required String chatMessageId, required String entryId}) async {
64	  _savedMessageEntryIds = {..._savedMessageEntryIds, chatMessageId: entryId};
65	  await _localCache.writeSavedMessageEntryIds(_savedMessageEntryIds);
66	}
67	```
68	
69	- **`savedEntryIdFor` is synchronous and does not itself await `_ensureLocalCacheLoaded()`.** It is only ever
70	  called by `ChatBloc._seedBookmarks`, strictly after `listMessages(sessionId)` has already resolved inside
71	  `_loadSession` — and `listMessages()` already awaits `_ensureLocalCacheLoaded()` unconditionally before
72	  returning, in both its success and (post-retry) failure paths. By the time `_seedBookmarks` runs, the map is
73	  therefore guaranteed populated. Calling `savedEntryIdFor` from anywhere that has *not* first awaited one of
74	  `createSession`/`listSessions`/`listMessages` would not have this guarantee — no such call site exists in
75	  this unit.
76	- **`recordMessageSaved` always persists**, even if the in-memory map already happened to contain the same
77	  pair (e.g. a retried save after a lost local record) — a harmless, idempotent overwrite.
78	
79	## Who depends on this
80	
81	`ChatBloc._seedBookmarks`/`_onBookmarkTapped` only (contracts/chat-bloc-bookmark-extension.md) — no other unit
82	yet calls `savedEntryIdFor`/`recordMessageSaved`.
83	
84	## Test scenarios this contract owns
85	
86	| # | Scenario | Expected |
87	|---|---|---|
88	| 1 | `readSavedMessageEntryIds()` with nothing ever written | `{}` |
89	| 2 | `writeSavedMessageEntryIds({'m1': 'e1'})` then `readSavedMessageEntryIds()` | `{'m1': 'e1'}` |
90	| 3 | `readSavedMessageEntryIds()` over corrupted/non-JSON stored data | `{}` (no throw) |
91	| 4 | `ChatRepositoryImpl.savedEntryIdFor('m1')` before any local-cache-loading call has ever run | `null` (the untouched initial `{}` — this is the expected pre-load state; `ChatBloc` never calls it in this state, see note above) |
92	| 5 | `listMessages(sessionId)` succeeds, then `savedEntryIdFor('m1')` where `'m1'` was previously recorded | returns the recorded `entryId`, confirming the local-cache load populated `_savedMessageEntryIds` as part of `_ensureLocalCacheLoaded()` |
93	| 6 | `recordMessageSaved(chatMessageId: 'm1', entryId: 'e1')` | `_localCache.writeSavedMessageEntryIds` is called with a map containing `{'m1': 'e1'}` merged with whatever was already in memory; a subsequent `savedEntryIdFor('m1')` returns `'e1'` without a new storage read |
94	| 7 | `recordMessageSaved` called twice for the same `chatMessageId` with the same `entryId` (simulating a retried save after a lost local record, research.md R1/FR-004) | Second call is a harmless overwrite — no error, map still has exactly one entry for that id |
95

